        "id": "2108608225704812894",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2015240852067540992/img/PGcuyJGPFsGB7-7Q.jpg"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 27.701,
            "height": 1440,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2015240852067540992/img/PGcuyJGPFsGB7-7Q.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2015240852067540992/vid/avc1/2560x1440/dZbw73C_FovHKgzi.mp4?tag=21",
            "width": 2560
          }
        ],
        "name": "X Freeze",
        "text": "Starlink is a life-saving technology that has helped save many lives during severe natural disasters\n\nSpaceX and Elon has repeatedly provided FREE Starlink connectivity to people affected by natural disasters and major infrastructure outages ❤️\n\nAs Elon Musk said:\n\n“Whenever there’s some sort of natural disaster somewhere, we always provide people with free Starlink internet connectivity”\n\nTraditional ground networks goes dark in a blink when severe natural disasters strike, leaving entire communities without communication and little they can do until connectivity is restored\n\nAnd that's where Starlink becomes a lifeline, keeping people connected when other networks fail, helping them reach safety, contact loved ones and communicate with emergency responders\n\nCommunication is one of the most important things when disasters hit. It can literally mean the difference between life and death\n https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2015241387160355077/video/1",
        "url": "https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2108608225704812894",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
